<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="4952d4bc">&lt;p&gt;
    Conduct the initial meeting with the project team and the client of the project.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conduct the team briefing session using the briefing materials.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Include the sponsor in the session. The sponsor can present, from the user perspective, an overview of the specific
        process under evaluation. This insight is especially important for identifying success criteria.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Document and follow up on any issues.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Discussion during this meeting can include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        An introduction of the project team and the various stakeholders involved on the client side, as well as a
        discussion of the roles of the individuals involved
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        An agreement between the project team and client as to the expectation and timeframe of the work to be accomplished
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Discussion of the risks and issues involved
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
